## Key Learnings

### 1. Standardization Precedes Automation

Before a process can be automated, decision criteria must be standardized.

### 2. Consistency Matters More Than Speed

Reliable decisions create more value than faster inconsistent decisions.

### 3. Explainability Builds Trust

Users are more likely to adopt systems whose outputs can be explained and audited.

### 4. Governance Enables Scale

Structured rules provide a scalable foundation for future automation initiatives.
